    "durationMs": 215778,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified.\n\n**What I built** — Laravel 11 (PHP 8.3) scaffolded via Composer and moved into `/workspace`, with:\n- `routes/api.php` registered via `apiPrefix: ''` in `bootstrap/app.php`, so paths are `/links`, `/links/{code}`, `/r/{code}`\n- `LinkController` + `Link` model + `links` migration (code unique index, atomic `clicks` counter)\n- Custom codes validated as 4–20 chars of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`, auto-generated codes otherwise; duplicate codes → 409, invalid/missing url, malformed JSON, or invalid code → 422, unknown codes → 404 — all with an `error` field via a global `ValidationException` JSON renderer\n- `.env` stripped of any `DB_*` values so all database settings come from the environment; `start.sh` runs `php artisan migrate --force` then `php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000 --no-reload` in the foreground; README documents startup\n\n**Verified end-to-end against MySQL** (`bench` database): 42/42 suite checks passed — URL returned byte-identical (query/fragment included), clicks as JSON integers, ascending list order with `total`, and a restart test confirming clicks and links persist. Also stress-checked 20 concurrent redirects: clicks incremented exactly 20 times.\n\nI stopped my test servers (port 8000 free) and reset the database with `migrate:fresh` so the automated suite starts from an empty `links` table."
  }
